## Files

```
Jarvis AI\
├── backend\
│   ├── server.py          FastAPI + WebSocket; streams tokens and audio
│   ├── brain.py           tool gating, prompt rules, deterministic pre-router
│   ├── tools.py           all 89 tools
│   ├── speech.py          Piper voice selection + speaking pace
│   ├── memory.py          SQLite: conversation history, user facts
│   ├── mobile.html        the phone UI (one file, no build step)
│   ├── data\              jarvis_memory.db, and last-output scratch files
│   ├── selftest_tools.py  runs every tool directly, tiered by risk
│   ├── test_commands.py   30 end-to-end "does it call the right tool" cases
│   ├── test_guards.py     73 adversarial confirmation-gate cases
│   ├── verify_ui.py       56 static checks on mobile.html
│   ├── test_ui.js         45 settings + chat tests   (needs: npm i jsdom)
│   ├── test_audio.js      19 gapless-audio tests     (needs: npm i jsdom)
│   └── test_handsfree.js  31 hands-free tests        (needs: npm i jsdom)
├── models\piper\          en_GB-alan-medium, en_GB-northern_english_male
├── jarvis-env\            the live virtualenv (Python 3.12)
├── memories.txt           full changelog and rationale
└── Notes                  this file
```

An earlier PC-microphone design (`main.py`, `stt.py`, `tts.py`,
`wake_word.py`, `brain_with_tools.py`) was deleted on 2026-09-22. It had been
dead since the switch to the phone as microphone, referenced APIs that no
longer exist, and would raise `AttributeError` if run. Recover from git history
if ever needed.

---

## Two mechanisms you must not accidentally remove

Both look odd and both exist for a measured reason. Read `memories.txt`
sessions 2, 6, 7 and 8 before touching them.

### 1. Two-turn confirmation, not a `confirm` parameter

Every destructive tool — `delete_path`, `shutdown_pc`, `restart_pc`,
`kill_process`, `empty_recycle_bin`, `claude_code_edit` — routes through
`tools._confirm_gate()`.

A `confirm: bool` parameter is **not** a safety gate. The model fills it in, and
qwen2.5:7b was observed setting `confirm=true` on its very first call and
editing a file nobody had approved. So `confirm` is absent from every schema,
and instead:

- the first call only **arms** the action and returns a message to relay
- it can only **run** on a *later* turn, and only if the user's own words were
  affirmative; an explicit refusal wins even inside a sentence containing "yes"
- the key identifies the exact action, so approving a shutdown cannot authorise
  a restart
- approval is single-use, a refusal clears it, and an armed action expires after
  `PENDING_TTL_TURNS` (3)

`test_guards.py` attacks all of this. If you change the gate, run it.

### 2. The deterministic pre-router

`brain.py` performs some tool calls **itself**, before the model generates,
because the model would not reliably make them:

| Case | Measured without the pre-router |
|---|---|
| world question → `web_answer` | 0 of 4 — answered from stale memory and *invented* citations ("according to NASA") |
| change request → `claude_code_edit` | 3 of 5 — silently produced prose instead |

Priority order per turn: refusal → confirmation replay → world lookup → arm an
edit. Results are handed to the model in a throwaway system message that is
**not** persisted, because `NUM_CTX` is 2048.

This does not bypass any safety gate; the gate is inside the tool and is
re-evaluated. The pre-router only guarantees the tool is *called*.

---

## Tools, by category

`files info power audio screen apps window input web media clipboard python
notify network weather dev recycle env memory speech devcode ai`

Registry, schemas and gating categories are kept at **89 / 89 / 89**. `brain.py`
prints a warning at import if they ever drift.

Path handling: `tools.resolve_path()` is the single funnel for all 14
path-taking tools. It resolves `my desktop`, `documents`, `downloads`, and this
project by many spellings (`Jarvis AI`, `JarvisAI`, `jarvis-ai`, `the project`),
handles compound paths like `my desktop/AI/Jarvis AI`, and **always returns an
absolute path**. When something is not found it reports *where it looked* — the
model used to invent a location otherwise.

---

## Speaking

- Say "talk faster", "slow down", "speak normally", or drag the pace slider.
  Range 0.6–1.7; internally the reciprocal of Piper's `length_scale`.
- Two voices installed. `en_GB-northern_english_male` is, despite its name,
  configured for Received Pronunciation.
- Voice and pace are **server** state, shared by every connected device.
- Audio is scheduled sample-accurately via Web Audio, so sentences run together
  with no gap. Verified under 1 ms deviation.

## The phone UI

Settings live behind the ⚙ button, which is in its own fixed layer that no
toggle can hide — hiding it would strand you in core-only mode. Holding the orb
also opens settings.

- **Layers**: text and labels / chat / mic controls, plus one-tap "core only"
- **Typography**: three typefaces, three text sizes
- **Conversation**: hands-free, and interrupt-by-voice
- **Speech**: pace slider, voice picker

Hands-free re-arms recognition manually after each turn. `continuous` stays
`false` — setting it true is what caused the Android duplication bug. After four
silent listens it pauses itself rather than looping forever.

Interrupt-by-voice is **off by default and needs headphones.** On a speaker the
mic hears the speaker. There is an echo guard that rejects heard text matching
what JARVIS just said, but it is a mitigation, not a fix.

---

## Running the tests

```powershell
cd "C:\Users\Home\Desktop\AI\Jarvis AI\backend"
..\jarvis-env\Scripts\python.exe verify_ui.py
..\jarvis-env\Scripts\python.exe test_guards.py
..\jarvis-env\Scripts\python.exe selftest_tools.py            # add --desktop --loud --ai
..\jarvis-env\Scripts\python.exe test_commands.py             # slow, uses the model
node test_ui.js ; node test_audio.js ; node test_handsfree.js # npm i jsdom first
```

298 checks pass as of 2026-09-22. The only expected failure is `docker_ps`,
when Docker Desktop is not running.

---

## Known limits

1. **Nothing has been verified on a real phone.** Every frontend test uses jsdom
   with a stubbed microphone and speaker. Gaplessness is proven numerically, not
   by ear; the echo guard is untested in a real room. **This is the biggest open
   gap.**
2. **No general web search.** DuckDuckGo's HTML endpoints now serve a CAPTCHA to
   this machine. `web_answer` uses DuckDuckGo instant answers and Wikipedia,
   which cannot answer technical or local questions — those are flagged, not
   faked. Set `BRAVE_API_KEY` and real web search starts working with no code
   change.
3. **RAM.** ~84% used with only the 7b model loaded.
4. `brightness_up`/`brightness_down` do nothing — the Asus VS197 has no DDC/CI.
   The tool says so plainly.
5. `ask_deepseek` and `ask_llama` fall back to an installed model;
   `ollama pull llama3.2:3b` for a genuinely different opinion.
6. The quick-tunnel URL changes on every restart. A fixed URL needs a domain.
7. The model still occasionally embellishes — e.g. naming a folder it was not
   told. Tool output is the source of truth; its paraphrase is not.

## Not built

Scheduled reminders, email, calendar, vision (screenshot → multimodal), wake
word, Home Assistant, Spotify API.
